ath11k: export the data-path ring layout for an NSS wifili probe

NSS's wifili offload wants the WLAN data-path rings described to it -
physical base, geometry and register bases for the TCL, TX completion,
REO destination, exception, release and reinject rings - so the UBI32
core can drive them directly instead of the host.

struct hal_srng already carries every field struct
nss_wifili_hal_srng_info asks for, down to HAL_SRNG_NUM_REG_GRP and
NSS_WIFILI_MAX_SRNG_REG_GROUPS_MSG both being 2.  Export a flat,
read-only copy of it so a separate module can build the init message
and find out whether the firmware accepts this description.

ath11k's behaviour is unchanged: the new file only reads rings that are
already set up, and the hook in core.c only records which ath11k_base
instances exist.  Keeping the translation out of tree avoids coupling
the backports build to qca-nss-drv's exports.

Diagnostic aid for bring-up, not for shipping as-is.

